# ripgrep's ignore file: keeps generated files and exact copies out of searches (rg and Claude Code's Grep tool honour
# it; git does not). The files stay where they are. CLAUDE.md lists what makes each one.
chroma-game/prototype/engine_pin/
chroma-game/prototype/web/index.html
chroma-game/prototype/web/page.html
chroma-game/prototype/web/src/ink-option-texts.json
chroma-game/prototype/rarity.py
chroma-library/earth.py
chroma-library/earth_art.py
chroma-library/earth_play.py
chroma-library/earth_politics.py
chroma-library/earth_science.py
chroma-library/earth_stage.py
chroma-art/game/lights.json
chroma-art/game/pics/
*.webp
# generated files with one line of 100 to 250 KB, which a search prints whole: the per-option icon map (made by
# web/src/live_icons.py) and the icon sprite (made by chroma-art/kit/glyph/build_icons.js), with their copies, and the
# icon set before it
option-icons-live.json
ink-icons.svg
chroma-art/old/
# In the shared folder (/mnt/project-files, where tools/mirror.py copies this file): run outputs, archives, the old
# game copies kept as rollbacks (each is also a release/ branch) and the game's staging copies (staging-next is the
# paused v23 game). Search one by naming it: rg <pattern> <folder>.
chroma-release/out/
chroma-engine/runs/
_archive/
chroma-game/prototype-v22/
chroma-game/prototype-v22.1/
chroma-game/staging-next/
chroma-game/staging-v22p1/
# and, also in the shared folder only: old built pages and samples with lines of up to 300 KB, the played lives that
# runs keep under notes/, and the Library's dated archive (scripts read it by path)
page.html
chroma-hud/impl/samples/
chroma-hud/impl/orig/
chroma-hud/mockup/
chroma-game/notes/**/lives/
chroma-library/archive/
